// Power-supply synthesis S2 (docs/spec/Power_Supply_Synthesis.md §3):
// no `using:` — the CHOOSER surveys every stdlib regulator, hard-gates on the
// datasheet capability attributes (v_out reachability, input range, load,
// the §4 linear-dissipation form, i_q), ranks the survivors by estimated
// regulator loss, and instantiates the winner. `bhdl … report` shows the
// full candidate survey with per-gate verdicts and computed numbers.
//
// 12V → 3.3V @ 1.5A, profile: balanced — every linear rejects on
// pass-element dissipation ((12−3.3)·1.5 ≈ 13W against ~2W packages); of
// the two qualifying bucks the LOWEST-LOSS part wins (TPS54331 0.30W vs
// LM2596 0.44W). `profile: cost` would rank by the real catalogue price of
// the regulator instead (see test_supply_ldo).

board SupplyAutoS2 {
    power VIN = 12V @ 3A;
    power VCC_3V3 = 3.3V @ 1.5A;
    ground GND;

    supply @VCC_3V3 from @VIN {
        ripple_max: 30mV;
        i_q_max:    5mA;
        profile:    balanced;
    }
}
